  "notes": "The West Coast anchor inside an East Coast production room, and his stated brief — keep the record from sounding East Coast — is the parameter that shapes everything here. Against the Bomb Squad layering around him his kit is fewer, drier and more spacious, so `kick.densityPerBar` and `percs.densityPerBar` are both cut below the g-funk parent and the hats sit at a lower `fillDensity`. The harmony is not a progression at all: his documented signature build is a looped bassline plus guitar, so `chords.impliedByRiff` is set and the chord part's variety is carried by `chordDurationBeats` and three harmonic rhythms rather than by chord changes. ⚠ The i–VII and i–iv families are INFERRED. The research names only the loop-modal form; they carry low weights and exist because the generated chord part still owes 55 distinct outputs over 200 seeds. Delete them first if this ever reads busier than the records. ⚠ `melody.timbreHint` is `clean_guitar` for the documented live guitar overdub; the live flute on the other track has no vocabulary entry and is modelled as the same part in a higher register. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates him high-medium — the workflow and role are interviewed, the specific tempo and harmony numbers are catalog-level. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 46 to 44 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 45 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 2.",
